    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="42" column="0" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="postProcessingLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Post processing</string>
     </property>
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">font-weight: bold;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="43" column="0" colspan="2">
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="deconvLayout">
     <item>
      <widget class="QCheckBox" name="deconvEnabledCheckBox">
       <property name="text">
        <string>matched deconvolution</string>
       </property>
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>SESSION068 - Approximate inverse of the KNOWN blur the downscale + bilinear upsample introduce on the splat buffer. Two Gaussian sources (the +0.3 low-pass on the 2D covariance diagonal, variance 0.3 texels^2; and the bilinear-tent kernel, variance 1/6), and the excess over scale 1 is undone by a discrete 5-point laplacian with an analytically derived strength: no per-scene tuning. Inert at buffer scale 1 by construction, so this checkbox does nothing there. Restores contrast lost to the upscale; cannot create detail the buffer does not carry.</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="deconvGainDoubleSpinBox">
       <property name="prefix">
        <string>gain </string>
       </property>
       <property name="decimals">
        <number>2</number>
       </property>
       <property name="minimum">
        <double>0.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="maximum">
        <double>10.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="singleStep">
        <double>0.050000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="value">
        <double>1.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>A/B multiplier on the analytically derived deconvolution strength. 1.0 = exactly as derived. Kept as a diagnostic knob to verify the derivation by eye: if the visually pleasing value is far from 1.0, the derivation is off, not the default. Result is clamped to the four-neighbour min/max regardless of gain, so this cannot ring by construction.</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item row="44" column="0" colspan="2">
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="rcasLayout">
     <item>
      <widget class="QCheckBox" name="rcasEnabledCheckBox">
       <property name="text">
        <string>RCAS sharpen</string>
       </property>
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>SESSION068 - AMD FidelityFX RCAS (MIT). A contrast-adaptive sharpen whose output is bounded by the four-neighbour min/max by construction, so it cannot ring or halo. Independent of the deconvolution above so either can be A/B tested alone or both applied together (deconvolution first, RCAS on top). Inert at buffer scale 1.</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="rcasSharpnessDoubleSpinBox">
       <property name="prefix">
        <string>sharpness </string>
       </property>
       <property name="decimals">
        <number>2</number>
       </property>
       <property name="minimum">
        <double>0.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="maximum">
        <double>1.000000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="singleStep">
        <double>0.050000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="value">
        <double>0.500000000000000</double>
       </property>
       <property name="toolTip">
        <string>RCAS sharpness, 0..1 - fraction of the algorithm's safe maximum lobe. 0 = mild, 1 = the strongest RCAS considers safe.</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item row="45" column="0" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="taaEnabledCheckBox">
     <property name="text">
      <string>temporal accumulation (TAA)</string>
     </property>
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>SESSION069 - Renders each frame with a subpixel jitter applied to the splat projection, and averages the resolved splat layer with previous frames' resolves.  In stillness the buffer converges to roughly full-frame quality over ceil(1/scale)^2 frames (about 4 at buffer scale 0.5).  Ghosting is impossible by construction: the scene is static (no motion vectors are ever needed) and the history counter is reset on ANY change - camera move, viewport/scale change, LoD apply, settings change, cloud add/remove.  Inert at buffer scale 1 (no sub-frame-pixel information to reconstruct) and while DoF weighted depth is on (the resolve needs to write gl_FragDepth in that mode, incompatible with drawing into a colour-only TAA target).</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="46" column="0" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="settingsPresetsSectionLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Settings presets</string>
     </property>
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">font-weight: bold;</string>
     </property>
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>Reset every control on this panel to its shipped default, or save/recall the panel's full current state under one of 5 session-local slots for A/B testing. See each control's own tooltip.</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="47" column="0" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QWidget" name="settingsPresetsWidget" native="true">
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="settingsPresetsHorizontalLayout">
      <property name="leftMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="topMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="rightMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="bottomMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <item>
       <widget class="QPushButton" name="resetToDefaultPushButton">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Reset to default</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Sets every control on this panel back to its shipped default value. Does not touch the presets below - each keeps whatever it last had saved into it.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QComboBox" name="presetComboBox">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Session-local preset slot. Picking one applies its saved panel state immediately (all 5 start out identical to the shipped defaults until you Save into one). Not persisted across an app restart - for A/B testing within a session.</string>
        </property>
        <item>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Preset1</string>
         </property>
        </item>
        <item>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Preset2</string>
         </property>
        </item>
        <item>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Preset3</string>
         </property>
        </item>
        <item>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Preset4</string>
         </property>
        </item>
        <item>
         <property name="text">
          <string>Preset5</string>
         </property>
        </item>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QPushButton" name="savePresetPushButton">
        <property name="text">
         <string>Save</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Writes every control's current value into the preset currently selected above, overwriting whatever was saved in it before.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="48" column="0" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="consoleLogsSectionLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Console logs</string>
     </property>
     <property name="styleSheet">
      <string notr="true">font-weight: bold;</string>
     </property>
     <property name="toolTip">
      <string>SESSION072: live toggles for stdout diagnostic traces - previously build-time consts that needed a rebuild to flip. Each print runs on the main thread and costs real frame time while it fires every frame during motion (measured) - leave off unless actively measuring something, and turn back off when done.</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="49" column="0" colspan="2">
    <widget class="QWidget" name="consoleLogsWidget" native="true">
     <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="consoleLogsHorizontalLayout">
      <property name="leftMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="topMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="rightMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <property name="bottomMargin">
       <number>0</number>
      </property>
      <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="filterLogCheckBox">
        <property name="text">
         <string>filter</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>[gsr-filter-kick] / [gsr-filter-drain] - kickOffFilters()/drainFilterResults(). Costs real frame time while it prints every frame during motion - main thread, flushed per line. Off by default.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="kickLogCheckBox">
        <property name="text">
         <string>kick</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>[gsr-kick] / [gsr-rot-blocked] - kickOffTraversals(). Same cost caveat as "filter" - off by default.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="QCheckBox" name="profLogCheckBox">
        <property name="text">
         <string>prof</string>
        </property>
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>[gsr-prof] - fillTraversalScratch() and the traversal-result VBO upload (session058). Same cost caveat as "filter" - off by default.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
   </item>
